b:
I think that the creation story is just that - a fanciful story, that has so many holes in it that it’s like a sieve.

I love the comedian. He does a really great YouTube video about the creation story as told in Genesis. The beauty of watching this is that it’s not some technical analysis by university professors... it is just down to earth logic and common sense with a huge dose of funny.

Not likely that you will get badly snapped for watching comedy either &lt;g&gt;

Let's analyze your fears and see if they are real. You say that all your "friends" are members of a specific religious group... yet you know that they will shun you and ignore your existence if you stop attending meetings. So these are not true friends, they are robots, controlled by the Borg. You are losing nothing, but you have an awful lot to gain.

&amp;#x200B;

I left the religious group at age 62. I lost a lifetime of these types of friends. I honestly do not miss a single one of them. They were all fakes. I now have friends who truly like me for who I am, and they know the real me. They take the time and effort to keep in touch and engage on more than a superficial (at the meetings) way.

&amp;#x200B;

You are young. Find out who you truly are inside and embrace that person. 

&amp;#x200B;

Do not let fear confine you. You will find heaps of great people if you just get out of the cult prison and allow yourself to grow and develop as a decent human being. You can do this. Look at the thousands of people who are on this sub and have done exactly what you are now faced with. They decided to live this life to the full, to follow their passions and dreams and not allow fear, obligation and guilt to turn them into a cult drone. You can do the same!
